$S(a)$ between the two points. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(a) & ={(a-4)}^{2}+{(2a-1-(-2))}^{2} \\\\  & =(a-4)^{2}+(2a+1)^{2} \\\\  & ={a}^{2}-8a+16+4{a}^{2}+4a+1 \\\\  & =5{a}^{2}-4a+17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want to minimize $S,$ we compute the derivative ${S}^{′}(a).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(a) & =10a-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe stationary points of $S(a)$ are the points where the derivative ${S}^{′}(a)=0.$ Solving this equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(a) & =0 \\\\ 10a-4 & =0 \\\\ a & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can see that ${S}^{″}(\\frac{2}{5})=10>0.$ So, the squared distance (and therefore the actual distance) reaches a minimum when $a=\\frac{2}{5}.$ \n\nSince $S(a)$ gives the squared distance between the two points, the actual distance $d$ between the two points when $a=\\frac{2}{5}$ is given by\n\n$$\nd=\\sqrt{S(\\frac{2}{5})}.\n$$\n\nComputing this quantity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{S(\\frac{2}{5})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{2}-4(\\frac{2}{5})+17} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{81}{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535587 true] [17592186356357 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356358 13194139535587 true] [17592186356357 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356359 13194139535587 true] [17592186356357 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356360 13194139535587 true] [17592186356357 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356361 13194139535587 true] [17592186356357 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356362 13194139535587 true] [17592186356357 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535587 true] [17592186356357 1041 "selection" 13194139535587 true] [17592186356357 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356362 13194139535587 true] [17592186356357 1110 #uuid "7c8d5b58-54ac-54ed-bb0b-b46c70c0b44b" 13194139535587 true] [17592186356358 1034 "\\sqrt{5}" 13194139535587 true] [17592186356358 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535587 true] [17592186356358 1111 #uuid "69520b36-52ae-5fd7-a274-674a9896939d" 13194139535587 true] [17592186356359 1034 "\\frac{2\\s